  "scope": "One disposable two-node Kind Kubernetes v1.36.1 cluster using Kind v0.32.0's bundled kindnet and its native NetworkPolicy implementation. Digest-pinned BusyBox Pods provide one synthetic training worker, harmless HTTP peers across two separate fixture namespaces, and an independent positive-control client/listener. Before/after ordinary IPv4 TCP/8080 requests show baseline reachability, an exact worker egress allowlist to one namespace-and-pod selector, denied namespace and Pod-label near misses, and an unaffected positive path plus one ordinary cross-node Pod TCP marker path. No RDMA, NCCL, GPU, encryption, VLAN/fabric enforcement, external traffic, DNS, IPv6, hostNetwork, or production workload is exercised.",
